# TypeScript shapes

Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes.

```ts
// ❌
type SongDTO = { id: number; name: string };

// ✅
interface SongDTO {
  id: number;
  name: string;
}
```

Use `type` only when `interface` cannot express it: unions, tuples, mapped types, or `z.infer<>`.
